course: dictionary
lesson: 9361
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Spoke is one of them. «She spoke to the teacher» shows spoke as the past of speak: she used her voice to talk.
explain: «An orb web is a wheel of strong spokes with a sticky spiral.» Here spoke is a thing, not an action. The words wheel and sticky spiral are the clues: a spoke is one of the thin lines that run from the middle of a wheel out to its edge.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask what the words around it are about. If they are about talking, a voice or a teacher, spoke is the past of speak. If they are about wheels, a rim or a web, a spoke is a thin line or bar. Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Spoke is the past form of speak: speak, speaks, spoke, spoken.
fact: «She spoke to the teacher.» Here spoke is a verb, something she did.
fact: A spoke is one of the thin bars or wires that join the hub (the middle) of a wheel to its rim.
fact: «A garden spider often eats its old web and builds a new one nearly every day.» The spokes are the dry lines that the spider walks on.
fact: Phrases to know: «spoke to», «spoke up», and «put a spoke in someone's wheel», which means to block or spoil someone's plan.
exercise: «She spoke to the teacher before lunch.» What does spoke mean here? | *Past form of speak: she used her voice to talk | A thin bar joining the hub to the rim of a wheel | Stood up quickly | Written down in a book
exercise: «An orb web is a wheel of strong spokes with a sticky spiral.» What is a spoke in this sentence? | The sticky spiral that catches insects | A person who talks loudly in a group | *A thin line running from the middle of the web out to its edge | A type of insect that lives in gardens
exercise: Find and copy the word that is the past form of speak: «Mum spoke softly as the baby slept.» | *spoke | baby | softly | slept
test: «The spider walked on the dry spokes so it never got stuck.» What does spokes mean? | *Thin lines running from the centre of the web to its edge | Sticky threads used to catch flies | People who talk in a meeting | Strings used to play a guitar
test: Yesterday Sam ___ to his friend about the football match. Which word fits the gap? | *spoke | speak | spoken | speaks
exam: Which sentence uses spoke in the same way as «The orb web is a wheel of strong spokes»? | Mia spoke softly to her dog | *Leo fixed the broken spoke on his bike wheel | The class spoke up together | Grandma has spoken to the vicar
